[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about what the safe set for θ = 120° might be.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me reconsider. The safe set needs to satisfy: for any triangle in [0m[38;2;124;124;124mS, and any cut, at least one resulting triangle is in S. This is a very strong [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcondition. Let me think about what triangles must be in S.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf (α, β, γ) ∈ S, then for any cut to any vertex with any parameter, at least [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mone of the two resulting triangles must be in S. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor a cut to vertex A with parameter x: T1 = (x, β, 180° - x - β) and T2 = (α - [0m[38;2;124;124;124mx, γ, x + β). At least one must be in S, for every x ∈ (0, α).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means: for every x ∈ (0, α), either (x, β, 180° - x - β) ∈ S or (α - x, γ, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mx + β) ∈ S.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a covering condition. For each x, at least one of the two triangles must[0m[38;2;124;124;124mbe in S.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, S must not contain any triangle with angle 120°. So:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (x, β, 180° - x - β) ∉ S if x = 120° or β = 120° or 180° - x - β = 120° (i.e.,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mx = 60° - β).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (α - x, γ, x + β) ∉ S if α - x = 120° (x = α - 120°) or γ = 120° or x + β = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m120° (x = 120° - β).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor the covering condition to hold, when both T1 and T2 have 120° (and thus [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mneither is in S), we need... well, the condition says at least one must be in S,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mbut if both have 120°, neither is in S, contradiction. So we need: there's no x [0m[38;2;124;124;124msuch that both T1 and T2 have 120°.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBoth T1 and T2 have 120°: this requires (x = 120° or β = 120° or x = 60° - β) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mAND (x = α - 120° or γ = 120° or x = 120° - β).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf β ≠ 120° and γ ≠ 120° (which must be the case for (α, β, γ) ∈ S):[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (x = 120° or x = 60° - β) AND (x = α - 120° or x = 120° - β)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCases:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. x = 120° and x = α - 120° → α = 240°. Impossible.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. x = 120° and x = 120° - β → β = 0. Impossible.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. x = 60° - β and x = α - 120° → α = 180° - β → γ = 0. Impossible.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. x = 60° - β and x = 120° - β → 60° = 120°. Impossible.[0m

